🐛 Describe the bug
Basically we don't guard that T is the class that we expect. We track the mutation on it and generate code to set x properly but I think we miss the case where the scope is the current script.
import torch

class T:
    def __init__(self, x):
        self.x = x

@torch.compile()
def fn(x):
    o = T(5)
    return o, x + 1

fn(torch.ones(1, 1))
T = 5
fn(torch.ones(1, 1))

